        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: unify Android Voice setup readiness",
        "body": "Closes #98268\n\nAI-assisted: yes. Sanitized transcript logs were not included.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAndroid Voice currently treats a connected Gateway as proof that both Realtime Talk and Dictation are ready. That produces false-ready UI when one selected provider is missing credentials, and it cannot represent mixed provider state.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nGateway `talk.catalog` now exposes provider registry aliases and resolves each row with the same canonical config ownership used by the runtime. Android consumes that response through one closed readiness model shared by Voice, Voice Setup, and permission continuations.\n\nThe rewrite removes the Android-owned alias table and parallel readiness flags from the original PR. Unknown catalog state remains non-blocking so a newer Gateway provider is still authoritative; confirmed missing setup routes to the existing settings flow. Realtime close failures also keep their specific status instead of being overwritten by a generic phase label.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRealtime Talk and Dictation can now show different, accurate readiness. A user can see that Google Live Voice needs setup while OpenAI Realtime Transcription is ready, and setup actions only block the affected mode.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rewritten exact head: `75d68797df`.\n- Gateway/protocol proof: 122 focused Vitest tests passed.\n- Android proof: readiness and Talk manager unit tests, ktlint, and Play debug APK assembly passed.\n- Repository proof: full build, docs MDX, native i18n, and whitespace checks passed.\n- Fresh maintainer autoreview completed with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Real source Gateway + Android emulator before/after proof: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/98269#issuecomment-4872525984\n\nThe live matrix used an intentionally non-production OpenAI credential. It proves catalog ownership, alias canonicalization, device pairing, Android routing, and mixed-state rendering; it does not claim a billed provider transcription turn.\n",
